    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-031: Float Layout (v1) + Stray Closing-Tag Fix** - the natural continuation of ADR-030's two honest deferrals.\n\n**Documentation only.** Implementation lands in a follow-up PR (Commit 1: float + stray fix; Commit 2: docs).\n\n## What this fixes\n\n| Bug | Before | After (expected) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Infobox rendering | Stacked inline list (.html / .htm / text/html / WHATWG / W3C) | **22em box at top-right** |\n| Stray closing tag | Visible in top-right of viewport | Hidden |\n\nBoth were documented in ADR-030's Implementation section as honest deferrals.\n\n## Measurement-driven scope\n\n### Float distribution in Wikipedia's CSS\n\n| Value | Count |\n|---|---|\n| float: right | 14 |\n| float: right + important | 1 |\n| float: left | 10 |\n| float: none | 7 |\n| float: none + important | 3 |\n| **Total** | **35** |\n\n**The target rule** (indented):\n\n    .infobox {\n        margin-left: 1em;\n        float: right;\n        clear: right;\n        width: 22em;   /* 352px at 16px root */\n    }\n\nbody.skin-minerva overrides (float:none important) do **not** match - we're not minerva skin. Clean target.\n\n### Why not :checked or position in this ADR\n\nAll 14 :checked rules drive dropdown open/close and radio widget state:\n\n- .vector-dropdown-checkbox:checked ~ .vector-dropdown-content - dropdowns\n- .cdx-radio__input:enabled:checked + .cdx-radio__icon - radio buttons\n\n**None affect the first viewport without user interaction.** Language dropdown is already hidden by ADR-029's workaround; user menu + page-tools dropdown are feature-flip-hidden by ADR-030.\n\n:checked also needs ~ (general sibling), visibility, opacity, :enabled, :focus, :active, :not(), box-shadow - a real ADR-032 chunk. Not urgent.\n\nposition (47 rules, 22 relative / 16 absolute / 3 fixed / 2 sticky) has no visible first-viewport driver either - ADR-030's measurement confirmed this.\n\n**Float is the last directly visible bug.** ADR-031 = float v1 + stray fix. ADR-032 = position + :checked + :not + clip + z-index + float v2.\n\n## Float v1 scope\n\n**In scope:**\n- Parse float: left | right | none\n- Floated children laid out at edge with natural/explicit width\n- Following block children **narrowed** when they start within the float's vertical extent (y_before < float_bottom)\n- clear parsed but treated as none (inert for the infobox case - nothing above it)\n\n**Deferred to ADR-032 v2:**\n- **Per-line text-wrap** (proper CSS behavior). Requires line-fragment-level float awareness in layout_inline_run - a ~200-250 line change to the most performance-sensitive path (line layout runs O(lines x fragments) on Wikipedia's 55k-line article).\n- Float stacking (multiple floats per band)\n- Full clear: left | right | both semantics\n\n**The v1 approximation**: paragraphs that **begin** within the float zone stay narrow even for lines below float_bottom. For the infobox case, all article intro lines are within the float's vertical extent - full narrowing is **visually identical** to proper per-line. Documented; measured in Commit 1.\n\n## Stray closing-tag fix\n\nCommit 1's diagnostic pinpoints the exact text node (path in DOM tree + content). Three cases:\n\n1. **Real text node from source** -> strip closing-tag-only text nodes during post-parse cleanup (~30 lines)\n2. **Lexbor artifact** -> fix in post-lexbor tree walk\n3. **Fix >100 lines** -> defer to own micro-cycle; ADR-031 ships float alone; documented in Commit 1's message\n\n## Expected visible delta (viewport 1774)\n\n| Check | Before ADR-031 | After ADR-031 (expected) |\n|---|---|---|\n| .infobox x | 324 (inline) | ~1042-1374 (right edge) |\n| .infobox width | 1398 (full content) | ~352 (22em) |\n| Infobox appearance | stacked list | proper box |\n| Article intro p width | 1398 | ~1014 (narrowed) |\n| Stray closing tag | visible | hidden |\n| vector-body y | 145 | 145 (unchanged) |\n\n## Two honest caveats in the spec\n\n1. **v1 uses block-narrowing, not per-line wrap.** Approximated. If v1's visual quality turns out unacceptable, ADR-032 v2 starts from working float infrastructure rather than a monolith. Same \"measure, ship, document honestly\" discipline as ADR-028/029/030.\n\n2. **Stray closing-tag fix size depends on diagnostic.** ADR-031 ships float regardless of whether the stray-tag fix lands in the same cycle.\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n\n- [ ] **Float v1 scope accepted** - block-narrowing (not per-line wrap) is the honest slice; v2 defers to ADR-032. Agree?\n- [ ] **:checked / position deferred again** - measurement shows no first-viewport driver. Confirm.\n- [ ] **Stray closing-tag fix is bundled (or deferred based on diagnostic)** - Commit 1 message documents which path applied. Acceptable?\n- [ ] **Infobox target rule is .infobox (22em / float:right / clear:right)** - no minerva override needed since we're not minerva skin. Confirm.\n\n## Test plan\n\nNo code touched (spec only). After merge: cmake --build build && ./build/tests/honeybee_tests - expect 399 / 1660 unchanged.\n\n## ADR\n\ndocs/decisions/031-float-layout.md - Status: Accepted; implementation in follow-up PR. Index row 031 added; reading order bumped to 008 through 031.\n\nRefs #169\n",
